---
fmContentType: glossaryEntry
term: "Tincture"
letter: "T"
anchor: "tincture"
category: "edibles"
---

A cannabis extract made by soaking decarboxylated cannabis in high-proof grain alcohol, then straining out the plant material. The alcohol dissolves and carries cannabinoids and terpenes into the liquid. Tinctures are the most precise, fast-acting edibles format — dosed in drops or millilitres, absorbed sublingually in 15–45 minutes, and usable in cooking or beverages. See also: Green Dragon, Golden Dragon, FECO.

→ [How to Make Cannabis Tincture](/edibles/how-to-make-cannabis-tincture-green-golden-dragon/)
